          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Higher Cartan geometry
            is supposed to be the generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            to
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+types"} geometric homotopy types
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"}> manifolds
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+stacks"} geometric stacks
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"} smooth infinity-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            of geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
            – the globalized version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Klein+geometry"} higher Klein geometry
            (see also the
            %a{:href => "#Survey"} survey table
            below).
          %p
            More in detail, this means that given a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \to G
            of suitably geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
            then a
            %em higher Cartan geometry
            modeled on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            is a higher geometric space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-stack"} geometric ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            etc. which, in some suitable sense, has its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+spaces"} tangent spaces
            identified with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
          %p
            Just like traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            (in particular in the guise of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
            = succeed "-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cartan23"}> Cartan 23
            ),
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+geometry"} conformal geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+geometry"} complex geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
          %p
            A class of examples where aspects of higher Cartan geometry may be seen to secretly underlie traditional discussion is the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma-models"} super p-brane sigma-models
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-spacetimes"} super-spacetimes
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SuperBraneGeometry"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Cartan+geometry"} super-Cartan geometry
          %p
            It is therefore maybe curious to note that while
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            as originating in (
            %a{:href => "#Cartan23"}> Cartan 23
            ) drew its motivation from the mathematical formulation of the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+gravity"} Einstein gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            such as 10d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            as well as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
          %h2#Motivation Motivation
          %p Here we informally survey motivation for higher Cartan geometry from phenomena and open problems visible in traditional geometry.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#MotivationPrequantizationOfSymplectic"} Pre-quantization of symplectic geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteParameterizationOfWZWTerms"} Higher pre-quantization and Parameterized WZW terms
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteGlobalizationOfWZWTerms"} Higher pre-quantization and Globalized WZW terms
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#MotivationSuperCartanGeometry"} Interlude: Super Cartan geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#HigherCartanConnectionsAndStackyCartanGeometries"} Higher Cartan connections and stacky Cartan geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DefiniteWZWTermsOnStackyCartanGeometries"} Definite higher WZW terms on stacky Cartan geometries
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Alternatively, higher Cartan geometry may be motivated intrinsically simply as the result of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+geometry"} synthetically
            formulating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Definition"} definition below
            proceeds. In the
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
            we discuss how this abstract theory indeed serves to inform the motivating phenomena listed here.
          %h3#MotivationPrequantizationOfSymplectic Pre-quantization of symplectic geometry
          %p
            While a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            is an example of an (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+G-structure"}> integrable
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+forms"} symplectic forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            are to be refined to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle-bundles+with+connection"} circle-bundles with connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            (with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\mathbf{L}} = \omega
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+prequantization"} geometric prequantization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mi pre
                      %mo −
                      %mi quantization
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (X,\omega) \stackrel{pre-quantization}{\mapsto} (X,\mathbf{L})
          %p
            While two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are either
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equal"} equal
            or not, two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be different and still
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            may have non-trivial
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            does not. (Readers may be more familiar with this kind of phenomenon from the discussion of the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
          %p
            Hence while there is just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            and hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+0-type"} homotopy 0-type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+forms"} symplectic forms
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            and hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-type"} homotopy 1-type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\nabla)
            involves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-types"} homotopy n-types
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mi ω
                            %mo }
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mo }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                          %mo −
                          %mi type
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\left\{ \omega \right\} &amp;&amp; \left\{ \mathbf{L} \right\}
                  \\\
                  0-type &amp;&amp; 1-type
                  }
          %p
            This implies notably that where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphism+group"} symplectomorphism group
            –,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            instead has a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+stabilizer+group"}> homotopy stabilizer group
            ”,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi Diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mi X
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mo ≃
                              %mi X
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi η
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %msup
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo *
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mo ≃
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                      %mo )
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Stab^h_{Diff(X)}(\mathbf{L})
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \\phi \colon X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} X\,,
                  \\\
                  \\eta \colon \phi^\ast \mathbf{L} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \mathbf{L}
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\right\}
          %p
            consisting of pairs of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^\ast \mathbf{L} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \mathbf{L}
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Stab
                            %mrow
                              %mi Diff
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi QuantMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Stab
                            %mrow
                              %mi Diff
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi SymplMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Stab^h_{Diff(X)}(\mathbf{L}) = QuantMorph(\mathbf{L})
                  \\\
                  Stab_{Diff(X)}(\omega) = SymplMorph(\omega)
                  }
          %p
            Hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+geometry"} prequantum geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathbf{L})
            is still clearly a geometry of sorts, but not a Cartan geometry. On the other hand, it is still similar enough to be usefully regarded form this perspective:
          %p
            Just like, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Darboux+theorem"} Darboux theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∧
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (V \simeq \mathbb{R}^{2n}, \omega_V = \mathbf{d}p_i \wedge \mathbf{d}q^i)
                  \\,,
          %p
            so every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            refining
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            over this atlas to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            given by the globally defined connection for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi V
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∧
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{V} \coloneqq p_i \wedge \mathbf{d}q^i
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, just like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(V,\omega_V)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
            under the canonical
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+stabilizer+group"} homotopy stabilizer group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_V
            (the part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QuantMorph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QuantMorph(\mathbf{L}_V)
            covering this) is the
            = succeed "-group," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mp%5Ec"} Mp^c
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Mp
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Mp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                        %mi ℤ
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mp^c(V,\omega_V) = Mp(V,\omega_V)\underset{\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}}{\times}U(1)
            = succeed "-version" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+group"} metaplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mp(V,\omega_V)
            ,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Stab
                            %mrow
                              %mi GL
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi V
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Mp
                            %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi QuantMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi SympMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Stab
                            %mrow
                              %mi GL
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi V
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_V)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \simeq
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  Mp^c(V,\omega_V)
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  QuantMorph(V,\mathbf{L}_V)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  Sp(V,\omega_V)
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  SympMorph(V,\omega_V)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \simeq
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; Stab_{GL(V)}(\omega_V)
                  }
          %p
            In this sense
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+quantization"} metaplectic quantization
            is a higher analog of symplectic geometry.
          %p
            While one may well reason, evidently, about pre-quantization of symplectic manifolds without a general theory of higher Cartan geometry in hand, this class of examples serves as a first blueprint for what higher Cartan geometry should be like, and points the way to its higher-degree generalizations considered
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteParameterizationOfWZWTerms"} below
          %p In particular, recurring themes are
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantization"} higher prequantizing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+forms"} definite forms
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %li
              %p
                their
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+stabilizer+groups"} homotopy stabilizer groups
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+quantomorphism+groups"} higher quantomorphism groups
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group+extension"} infinity-group extension
                they form and the higher
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
                associated with them.
          %h3#MotivationDefiniteParameterizationOfWZWTerms Higher pre-quantization and Parameterized WZW terms
          %p
            A particularly interesting example of a pre-quantization as above is the Kac-Moody
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+groups"} loop groups
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "loop+group#ByGeometricQuantization"} here
          %p
            Loop groups are naturally symplectic geometries, whose symplectic form is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+form"} left invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} differential 3-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_3 = \langle-,[-,-]\rangle
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi transgression
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (G, \omega_3)
                  \\stackrel{transgression}{\mapsto}
                  (L G, \omega_2)
          %p
            Similarly their central extension is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            of a higher-degree analog of traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-quantization"} pre-quantization
            down on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+form"} left invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} differential 3-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_3 = \langle-,[-,-]\rangle
            lifts to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            3-form is
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\mathbf{L}_3} = \omega_3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi transgression
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (G, \mathbf{L}_3)
                  \\stackrel{transgression}{\mapsto}
                  (L G, \mathbf{L}_2)
          %p
            This
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_3
            is also called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+gerbe"} WZW gerbe
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %em WZW term
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+holonomy"} volume holonomy
            serves as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+interaction"} gauge interaction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+sigma+model"} Wess-Zumino-Witten sigma model
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Now the 2-connections on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            hence a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-type"} homotopy 2-type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G,\nabla^G)
            may be regarded as being an object in yet a bit higher differential geometry.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 3
                            %mo }
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mn 3
                            %mo }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                          %mo −
                          %mi type
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mn 2
                          %mo −
                          %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\left\{ \omega_3 \right\} &amp;&amp; \left\{ \mathbf{L}_3 \right\}
                  \\\
                  0-type &amp;&amp; 2-type
                  }
          %p
            Now given a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mn 3
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mn 3
                            %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{L}_3 &amp;&amp; \mathbf{L}_3^P
                  \\\
                  G &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  }
          %p
            then a natural question is whether there is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+term"} definite parameterization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_3^P
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_3
            to a 2-form connection on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            which restricts fiberwise to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla^G
            in a suitable sense up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+terms"} parameterized WZW terms
            play a key role in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %p
            One finds that such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+term"} definite parameterizations
            are equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift+of+structure+group"} lifts of structure group
            of the bundle from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+stabilizer+group"} homotopy stabilizer group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_3
            under the right
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi String
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String(G)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of the group of based paths of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            by the Kac-Moody loop group of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+2-group"} Heisenberg 2-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Stab
                    %mi G
                    %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mi G
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Heis(\mathbf{L}_3)
                  \=
                  Stab^h_{G}(\mathbf{L}_3)
                  \\simeq
                  String(G)
                  \\simeq
                  (P_\ast G) // \widehat{L G}
          %p
            Hence a definite parameterization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_3
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to that is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo =
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = SU(N)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} c
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \c_2(P)
            %li
              %p
                for
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo =
                        %mi Spin
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Spin
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{2}p_1(P)
          %p
            These are the obstructions famous from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly+cancellation"} Green-Schwarz anomaly cancellation
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
          %p
            While this class of examples is not yet Cartan geometry proper (higher or not) since the bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            here is not a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+model"} definite parameterizations
            of higher pre-quantized forms related to higher
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
            %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteGlobalizationOfWZWTerms"} below
            and key ingredients of higher Cartan geometry apply to both cases.
          %p
            But more generally, one considers this situation for WZW terms on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+WZW+model"} gauged WZW model
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %h4#goal_1_of_higher_cartan_geometry Goal 1 of higher Cartan geometry
            %p
              Provide
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
              classes for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+parameterizations+of+higher+WZW+terms"} definite parameterizations of higher WZW terms
          %p
            This we consider
            %a{:href => "#ObstructionClassesForDefiniteParameterizations"} below
          %h3#MotivationDefiniteGlobalizationOfWZWTerms Higher pre-quantization and Globalized WZW terms
          %p
            Often one wants to consider definite parameterizations as above along the tangent bundle of a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em global
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalization+of+a+WZW+term"} definite globalization of a WZW term
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            equipped with a (constant, i.e. translationally
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+form"} left invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential (p+2)-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega_V \in \Omega^{p+2}(V)
          %p
            a natural question to ask is for a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (i.e. an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \simeq \mathbb{R}^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \in \Omega^2(X)
          %p
            which is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+form"} definite form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            is equal, up to a
            = succeed "-transformation," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
          %p
            Standard theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
            easily shows that such definite forms correspond to
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Stab
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab_{GL(V)}(\omega_V)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab_{GL(V)}(\omega_V)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
            under the canonical
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            (by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
          %p
            For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{R}^7
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V \in \Omega^3(V)
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab_{GL(V)}(\omega_V) = G_2
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
            and this yields
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-structures"} G₂-structures
          %p
            But in view of the
            %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteParameterizationOfWZWTerms"} above
            discussion one is led to re-state this question for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\omega_V)
            is refined to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum (p+1)-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\mathbf{L}_{p+2})
          %p
            Just as a 1-connection is precisely the data needed to define
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} line holonomy
            = succeed "-connection" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+holonomy"} volume holonomy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mo }
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mo }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                          %mo −
                          %mi type
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\left\{ \omega_{p+2} \right\} &amp;&amp; \left\{ \mathbf{L}_{p+2} \right\}
                  \\\
                  0-type &amp;&amp; (p+1)-type
                  }
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalization"} definite globalization
            of such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{p+2}
            over a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            should be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle (p+1)-connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{p+1}^X
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which suitably, up to the relevant
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_V
          %p
            For instance for first-order integrable such globalizations one would require that (in particular) for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔻
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}
            in a
            = succeed "-cover" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            we have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi 𝔻
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                            %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi 𝔻
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔻
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                            %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; \mathbf{L}_{p+2}|_{|\mathbb{D}} &amp; \simeq &amp; \mathbf{L}_{p+2}^X|_{|\mathbb{D}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{D}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; U &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  V &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{L}_{p+2} &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \mathbf{L}_{p+2}^X
                  }
          %p
            This problem indeed appears in the formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma+models"} super p-brane sigma models
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-spacetimes"} super-spacetimes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
            is an exceptional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} cocycle
            of degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+2)
            and the formulation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
            requires that it is refined (higher pre-quantized) to a higher WZW term, a
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            imply a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalization"} definite globalization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-spacetime"} super-spacetime
            = succeed "-connection," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+anomaly"} classical anomaly
          %p
            These
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalizations"} definite globalizations
            are in particular
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+term"} definite parameterizations
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi 𝔻
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi L
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                            %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi T
                                %mi inf
                              %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔻
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mi inf
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{L}_{p+2}|_{|\mathbb{D}} &amp;&amp; \mathbf{L}_{p+2}^X|_{T_{inf}X}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{D} &amp; \longrightarrow&amp; T_{inf}X
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  }
          %p
            Notice that for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
            every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+transformation"} linear transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔻
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Aut(\mathbb{D}) \simeq GL(V)
          %p
            and therefore by the above a definite globalization determines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Stab
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to such a structure is an obstruction to a definite globalization.
          %p
            This construction extends to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            (an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi definite
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi globalizations
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msubsup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                              %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi of
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi over
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi X
                    %mo }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Stab
                              %mrow
                                %mi GL
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi V
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi 𝔻
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo −
                            %mi structures
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi on
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi X
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  definite \; globalizations \; \mathbf{L}_{p+2}^X
                  \\\
                  of\; \mathbf{L}_{p+2} \; over \; X
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2}|_{\mathbb{D}})-structures
                  \\\
                  on \; X
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (For instance in the case of applications to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            that we turn to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationSuperCartanGeometry"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
          %p
            It is here that developing a theory of higher Cartan geometry has much potential, since, while the globalizations of the forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_V
            have been extensively studied in the literature, the globalization of their pre-quantized refinement to higher WZW-terms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{p+2}
            has traditionally received almost no attention yet. A brief mentioning of the necessity of considering appears for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten86"}> Witten 86, p. 17
            ), but traditional tools do get one very far in this question.
          %p
            More precisely, this is the situation for all those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            in the old
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            which have no tensor-multiplets on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            or the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and not the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationSuperCartanGeometry"} below
          %p
            Accordingly, now the symmetries of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{p+2}^X
            form an extension of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
            of the induced
            = succeed "-structure." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Stab
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi 𝔻
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2}|_{\mathbb{D}})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi p
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi FlatConn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi Diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Isom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathbf{B}^p U(1))FlatConn(X)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Stab^h_{Diff(X)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2}^X)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Isom(X)
          %p
            One finds that after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            these extensions are of the kind konwn in the phyiscs literature as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+charge"} BPS charge
            extensions.
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %h3#goal_2_of_higher_cartan_geometry Goal 2 of higher Cartan geometry
            %p
              Classify these refined and generalized
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
          %p This we turn to belowsometryGroups).
          %p So far these examples point to higher Cartan geometry modeled on homomorphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⋊
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2})
                  \\longrightarrow
                  V \rtimes Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2})
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+stabilizer+group"} homotopy stabilizer group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab^h_{GL(V)}(\mathbf{L}_{p+2})
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is still an ordinary manifold. We now turn (
            %a{:href => "#HigherCartanConnectionsAndStackyCartanGeometries"}> below
            ) to examples that also turn the local model space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            into an higher
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+type"} geometric homotopy type
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationSuperCartanGeometry"} interlude
          %h3#MotivationSuperCartanGeometry Interlude: Super-Cartan geometry
          %p
            Before further motivating ever higher Cartan geometry, it serves to pause and realize that while passing from manifolds to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            itself, which leads to Cartan geometry in the generality of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
            other than that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            –
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Cartan+geometry"} super-Cartan geometry
          %p
            One key example for this is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structures"} orthogonal structures
            encoding (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+geometry"}> pseudo
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            of particular relevance in the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            serve to set up the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %p
            More in detail, after picking a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in \mathbb{N}
            and writing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            %a{:href => "spin+representation#RealIrreducibleSpinRepresentationInLorentzSignature"} real spin representation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mi even
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mi N
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mi odd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\underbrace{\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})}_{even} \oplus \underbrace{N}_{odd}
          %p
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            in odd degree becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            by letting the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi even
                  %mo ,
                  %mi odd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [even,odd]
            bracket to be given by the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            and by letting the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi odd
                  %mo ,
                  %mi odd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [odd,odd]
            bracket be given by a canonically induced bilinear and
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{o}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+Lie+algebra"} Lorentz Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{o}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi 𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})/\mathfrak{o}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})
          %p
            is called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            (equipped with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+Lie+algebra"} super translation Lie algebra
            structure).
          %p
            From this, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Cartan+geometry"} super-Cartan geometry
            is defined in direct analogy to the Cartan formulation of Riemannian geometry
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔥
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h}
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi 𝔥
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}/\mathfrak{h}
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+geometry"}> pseudo-Riemannian geometry
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+gravity"} Einstein gravity
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{o}(d-1,1)
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert N})
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{o}(d-1,1)
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert N}
          %p
            Indeed, all the traditional literature on supergravity (e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre91"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91
            )) is phrased, more or less explicitly, in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connections"} Cartan connections
            for the inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            into the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
          %p
            It so happens that from within such super-Cartan geometry there appear some of the most interesting examples of what should be higher Cartan geometry, hence
            = succeed "." do
              %em higher super-Cartan geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteGlobalizationOfWZWTerms"} below
          %h3#HigherCartanConnectionsAndStackyCartanGeometries Higher Cartan connections and Stacky Cartan geometries
          %p
            A traditional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            satisfying some extra conditions, is locally (on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} chart
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} Lie algebra valued differential form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(U,\mathfrak{g})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(U) \longleftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) \colon A
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebras"} graded algebras
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(U) \longleftarrow CE(\mathfrak{g}) \colon A
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_A
            to vanish, hence to the connection being a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
          %p
            In particular for the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetimes"} superspacetimes
            one considers this for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} = \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1|N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
            as for ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            modeled by ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            field.
          %p
            In detail, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{10,1|N=1}))
            for 11-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            turned super via the unique irreducible 32-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "spin+representation#RealIrreducibleSpinRepresentationInLorentzSignature"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+commutative+algebra"} graded commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            on
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi a
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 11
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^a\}_{a = 1}^{11}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega^{ a b}\}
                of degree
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
            %li
              %p
                and elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi α
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 32
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi^\alpha\}_{\alpha = 1}^{32}
                of degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
          %p
            and as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} differential graded algebra
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi CE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{CE}
            is determined by the equations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi CE
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE} \, \omega^{a b} = \omega^a{}_b \wedge \omega^{b c}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi CE
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mi i
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %mi ψ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE} \, e^{a } = \omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b + \frac{i}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^a \psi
                  \\,.
          %p
            An algebra homomorphism as above sends these generators to differential forms of the corresponding degree, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi a
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^a \coloneqq A(e^a) \in \Omega^{(1,even)}(U)
                  \\,,
          %p
            whe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{a}{}_{b} \coloneqq A(\omega^a{}_b) \in \Omega^{(1,even)}(U)
          %p
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi^\alpha \coloneqq A(\psi^\alpha) \in \Omega^{(1,odd)}(U)
                  \\,.
          %p
            But a key aspect of higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            theories is that their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            content necessarily includes, in addition to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential n-form
            fields, notably the 2-fom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            of 10-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            as well as the 3-form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
          %p
            This means that these higher dimensional supergravity theories are not in fact entirely described by super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"}> Cartan geometry
            \. This is to be contrasted with the fact that the very motivation for Cartan geometry, in the original article (
            %a{:href => "#Cartan23"}> Cartan 23
            ), was the mathematical formulation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"}> general relativity
            ).
          %p
            Now a key insight due to (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFreRegge80"}> D’Auria-Fré-Regge 80
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"} D’Auria-Fré 82
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
          %p Namely, we may add to the above CE-algabra
          %ul
            %li
              a single generator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_3
              of degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mi even
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (3,even)
          %p and extend the differential to that by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi CE
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE} \, c_3 = \frac{1}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^{a b} \wedge \psi \wedge e_a \wedge e_b
                  \\,.
          %p
            This still squares to zero due to the remarkable property of 11d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            by which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi CE
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^{a b} \wedge \psi \wedge e_a \wedge e_b \in CE^4(\mathfrak{Iso}(10,1|N=1))
            is a representative of an exception
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            class. (The collection of all these exceptional classes constitutes what is known as the
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
          %p
            In the textbook (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre91"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91
            ) a beautiful algorithm for constructing and handling higher supergravity theories based on such generalized CE-algebras is presented, but it seems fair to say that the authors struggle a bit with the right mathematical perspective to describe what is really happening here.
          %p
            But from a modern perspective this becomes crystal clear: these generalized CE algebras are CE-algebras not of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            but of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+homotopy+Lie+algebra"} strong homotopy Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"} L-infinity algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-algebras"} Lie (p+1)-algebras
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
            the degree of the relevant differential form field.
          %p
            Specifically, we may write the above generalized CE-algebra with the extra degree-3 generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_3
            as the CE-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔪
                  %mn 2
                  %mi 𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{m}2\mathfrak{brane})
          %p
            of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔪
                    %mn 2
                    %mi 𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m}2\mathfrak{brane}
          %p Now a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔪
                  %mn 2
                  %mi 𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(U) \stackrel{}{\longleftarrow} CE(\mathfrak{m}2\mathfrak{brane}) \;\colon\; A
          %p
            encodes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            fields as above, but in addition it encodes a 3-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_3 \coloneqq A(c_3) \in \Omega^{(3,even)}(U)
          %p
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_4 = \mathbf{d}C_3 + \frac{1}{2}\bar \Psi \Gamma^{a b} \wedge \Psi \wedge E_a \wedge E_b
          %p
            satisfies a modified
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
            ).
          %p
            So this collection of differential form data is no longer a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} Lie algebra valued differential form
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+valued+differential+form"} L-infinity algebra valued differential form
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
          %p The quotient
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ^
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝔪
                  %mn 2
                  %mi 𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi 𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widehat{\mathbb{R}}^{10,1|N=1}
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\mathfrak{g}/\mathfrak{h}
                  \=
                  \\mathfrak{m}2\mathfrak{brane} / \mathfrak{o}(\mathbb{R}^{10,1|N=1})
          %p
            is known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-group"} smooth 3-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            which receives a map from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
          %p
            This means that a global description of the geometry which (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre91"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91
            ) discuss locally on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
            has to be a higher kind of Cartan geometry which is locally modeled not just on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosets"} cosets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-group"}> smooth
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+infinity-groupoid"} supergeometric
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
          %h3#DefiniteWZWTermsOnStackyCartanGeometries Definite higher WZW terms on stacky Cartan geometries
          %p
            Once such a higher Cartan super-spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as
            %a{:href => "#HigherCartanConnectionsAndStackyCartanGeometries"} above
            has been obtained, then we are back to the
            %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteGlobalizationOfWZWTerms"} above
            question of constructing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalizations+of+WZW+terms"} definite globalizations of WZW terms
            over it.
          %p
            Indeed, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma-models"} super p-brane sigma-models
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+terms"} WZW terms
            defined not on plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} extended super Minkowski spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            sigma model is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantization"} higher prequantization
            of the following 7-form (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 5
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 5
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 13
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi CE
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ^
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega_7
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\frac{1}{2} \bar \psi \wedge \Gamma^{a_1 \cdots a_5} \psi \wedge e_{a_1} \wedge \cdots \wedge e_{a_5}
                  +
                  \\frac{13}{2} \bar \psi \Gamma^{a_1 a_2} \psi \wedge e_{a_1} \wedge e_{a_2} \wedge c_3
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\in
                  CE^7(\widehat{\mathbb{R}}^{10,1|N=1})
          %p
            on the above
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_3
            is the extra degree-3 generator discussed above.
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            this becomes (
            %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
            ) a degree-7 WZW term defined on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+infinity-groupoid"} supergeometric 3-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            and defining the M5-brane sigma model on a curved supergravity target space means to construct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalizations"} definite globalizations
            of this over higher Cartan geometries
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            modeled on this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
          %p
            The result
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mn 7
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathbf{L}^X_7)
            is a pair which is still analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometries
            that we started with, but is now in higher geometric homotopy theory in every possible sense.
          %p
            Computing for this case the higher extensions of isometries as
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationDefiniteGlobalizationOfWZWTerms"} above
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#dcct"} dcct, sections 1.2.11.3 and 1.2.15.3.3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+n-group"} quantomorphism n-group
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+infinity-groupoid"} supergeometric 7-group
            with is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+Lie+algebra"} M-theory Lie algebra
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            being a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"}> BPS state
            ” of 11d supergravity. These BPS states are known to be an immensely rich mathematical topic (e.g. via their “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wall+crossing"} wall crossing
            phenomena”), but one sees here that it is but the local and infinitesimal shadow of a much richer structure: higher isometries in higher super-Cartan geometry.
          %p
            In terms of the physics this refinement corresponds to
            = succeed "-cancellation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+anomaly"} classical anomaly
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma+models"} super p-brane sigma models
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %h4#goal_3_of_higher_cartan_geometry Goal 3 of higher Cartan geometry
            %p
              Provide
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+anomaly"} classical anomaly
              cancellation for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma-models"} super p-brane sigma-models
              such as the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
          %h2#Definition Definition
