          %h3#SuperBraneGeometry
            Super-Poincaré-geometry, Super
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            Notice that ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            can be understood as the theory of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (O(d,1) \hookrightarrow Iso(d,1))
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(d,1)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+group"} Poincare group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(d,1)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+formulation+of+gravity"} first order formulation of gravity
          %p
            One can read the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
            as saying that higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            is analogously given by higher Cartan supergeometry. See there and see the examples at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Klein+geometry"} higher Klein geometry
            for more on this.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Klein+geometry"} higher Klein geometry
          %h2#references References
          %p Traditional Cartan geometry goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Cartan23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89lie+Cartan"} Élie Cartan
              = succeed "." do
                %em Sur les variétés à connexion affine et la théorie de la relativité généralisée (première partie)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=ASENS_1923_3_40__325_0"} NUMDAM
          %p
            There is secretly a good bit of higher super-Cartan geometry in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            textbook
          %ul
            %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
          %p based on results and observations due to
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFreRegge80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tullio+Regge"} Tullio Regge
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Graded Lie algebra, cohomology and supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/156191"} spire
            %li#DAuriaFre82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravity.pdf", :title => "Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup"} Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup
          %p
            Mentioning of the need for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalizations+of+WZW+terms"} definite globalizations of WZW terms
            is (ever so briefly) in
          %ul
            %li#Witten86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , p. 17 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twistor - Like Transform in Ten-Dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/214192/?ln=en"} spire
          %p
            That there ought to be a systematic study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Klein+geometry"} higher Klein geometry
            and higher Cartan geometry has been amplified by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David Corfield
            since 2006.
          %p
            Construction of the higher WZW terms on homotopy quotients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            of higher super-groups is due to
          %ul
            %li#FSS13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"} arXiv:1308.5264
          %p
            with more details in (
            %a{:href => "#dcct"}> dcct
            ).
          %p
            A formalization of higher Cartan geometry via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            is in
          %ul
            %li#dcct
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Cartan+Geometry"} Higher Cartan Geometry
          %p
            Formalization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+homotopy+type+theory"} modal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#Wellen17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Wellen"}> Felix Wellen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/thesis+Wellen"} Formalizing Cartan Geometry in Modal Homotopy Type Theory
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré duality
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            (cf. also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartan+geometry"} super Cartan geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konstantin+Eder"}> Konstantin Eder
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simone+Noja"} Simone Noja
              %em Poincaré Duality for Supermanifolds, Higher Cartan Structures and Geometric Supergravity
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.05224"}> arXiv:2312.05224
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
